  <PosterCell span={6} landscapeSpan={12} marker="7" kicker="Takeaway" title="Attach recovery affordances at the point of failure" fill>
    <ol class="poster-body takeaway-list">
      <li>Silent failures need an <strong>in-band signal</strong>: fault-aware prompts and extended reasoning budgets do not substitute for the receipt.</li>
      <li>Put <span class="oc-main">recovery tools</span> in the receipt: diagnostics without them perform at baseline in our controls.</li>
      <li>Keep it <strong>nonbinding and cheap</strong>: +$0.13 (+7%) per episode with no extra model call beats a five-call reviewer port (+$9.24, +498%) by +11.25 points.</li>
      <li>Expect gains where the fault <strong>blocks completion</strong> (baseline ≤ 16%); elsewhere rescues and harms roughly cancel.</li>
      <li>Detection stops at the <span class="oc-flag">learned rule classes</span>: corruption inside plausible strings mostly slips through. Extending it is open.</li>
    </ol>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={12} landscapeSpan={12} marker="8" kicker="TL;DR">
    <div class="tldr-band poster-body">
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What we did</p>
        <p>
          Outcome Monitors check tool results against <strong>rules learned from clean
          traces</strong> or public schemas. On a violation they keep the result and append a
          <span class="oc-main">nonbinding receipt</span>: violated property, witness, and recovery
          tools. Frozen, prespecified evaluations with injected failures.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What we found</p>
        <p>
          ToolMaze completion rises <strong>10.9% → 28.1%</strong> across four models in two families
          and replicates in a third; τ-bench retail improves +14.0 / +12.0 points. Ablations identify
          the <strong>recovery-tool list</strong>, not diagnostic detail or timing, as the active
          content.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What you should do</p>
        <p>
          When a tool result can be silently wrong, <strong>deliver recovery options with the
          flag</strong>: a one-line in-band receipt outperforms a 5-call reviewer at 1/70th the added
          cost. And treat the contract vocabulary as the boundary of trust: outside it, detection
          drops to 46%.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tldr-qr">
        <img src="/poster/outcome-monitors-online-qr.svg" alt="QR code linking to this poster online at spanthi.com" />
        <p class="tldr-qr-label">This poster online</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </PosterCell>
